<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Andalus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Andalus was the name given to the parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a> under Muslim rule from 711 until 1492. It was conquered under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> and later ruled by an independent Umayyad dynasty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, outside Abbasid control. In the eleventh and twelfth centuries the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> intervened from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> to rule it and defend it against the Christian kingdoms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-andalus.jpg" alt="al-Andalus" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Al-Andalus732.jpg:Q4767211492~commonswiki (talk · contribs) EmiratoDeCórdoba910.svg:rowanwindwhistler (talk · contrib... · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al-Andalus732.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
